<p>Inside the structure, Calel has placed a sculpture of a turtle with corn=
 breaking through its shell. In Maya cosmology, the turtle, with its rounde=
d shell, represents the earth and its time cycles, and corn not only symbol=
izes the element from which humanity was first formed but also is the centr=
al sustaining force of Maya life. On the outside, a mountain of ceramic cor=
n implies abundance and security.<br class=3D"softbreak"></p>

